From 880d7bc2a9570e5250110ad2372c5aaaea1a4bfa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AssemblyP1 Agent <agent@assemblyp1.local>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 13:17:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] w-3b8e15: rebuild the substitution cost on articulatory
 features

Replaces phonetics::distance between single codepoints with a feature
distance over the corpus symbol inventory: a place/manner/voicing triple
for consonants, a height/backness/rounding/reduction vector for vowels,
with weights ordered by how reliably a listener recovers each cue, and a
discount when either side is a reduced vowel. General over symbol classes;
no word or phrase appears anywhere in the rule.

Measured on the canonical segmentation via MADGAB_TRACE_SPANS/WORDS:
  hits 0.20  justice 0.00  dupe 0.15->0.10  hid 0.3695->0.265  came 0.40->0.10
  total 1.1195 -> 0.6650

came now costs a substitution at slot rank 0 instead of a 0.40
delete+insert detour around a codepoint artifact. The phrase is still not
enumerated (15484 candidates, absent), so the residual 0.665 is now
dominated by the two flat GAP_COSTs for the h insertions.
